<title>MEXICO: RESEARCH ALERT - Comerci cut.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Comerci cut.</headline>
<text>
<p>-- ING Barings analyst Sebastian Barry-Taylor has cut his rating for Mexican retail chain Controladora Comercial Mexicana SA to hold from buy.</p>
<p>-- In an April 28 report, he wrote in part: &quot;The company's balance sheet has deteriorated compared with 4Q96, margins are the lowest in the sector and confidence in management is still low.</p>
<p>-- &quot;The stock is trading at 31.9 adjusted (estimated 1997) earnings. The sector offers better alternatives with lower risk.&quot;</p>
<p>-- The company's American Depositary Receipts were unchanged at 15-1/4 with no trades recorded.</p>
<p>((--Ian Simpson, Wall Street desk, (212) 859-1879))</p>
</text>
